From: Chromium-HaikuOS contributors
Subject: [PATCH] ui: Haiku native window frame, Wayland compatibility and input

Haiku's in-process Wayland server (HaikuPorts wayland_server) implements
the core protocols on top of the Haiku API, but is older than the
protocol level Chromium 156 expects and offers a different set of
extensions.

- Native window frame. Haiku's server draws real Haiku decorations (tab,
  close and zoom buttons, borders) when a client asks for server-side
  decorations through the KDE server-decoration protocol; it does not
  offer xdg-decoration. Add the org_kde_kwin_server_decoration protocol
  target, bind its manager in WaylandConnection, use it in XdgToplevel
  when xdg-decoration is absent (request_mode SERVER/CLIENT, mode event
  updates decoration_mode_), report server-side decoration support from
  OzonePlatformWayland, and default "Use system title bar and borders" to
  on for Haiku (custom_frame_pref_default = false).
- wayland_object.*, wayland_connection.*: Haiku's libwayland lacks the
  wl_fixes interface (wl_registry destruction, ack of global removal);
  those calls are compiled out on Haiku.
- wayland_keyboard.cc: WL_KEYBOARD_KEY_STATE_REPEATED is defined for the
  older protocol headers.
- wayland_pointer.cc: no axis_relative_direction event in Haiku's
  wl_pointer version.
- events/keycodes/dom/keycode_converter.*: use the evdev key code tables
  on Haiku as on FreeBSD (Wayland sends evdev codes).
- gfx/linux/dmabuf_uapi.h: Linux _IOC encodings for the dma-buf ioctl
  numbers (only built, never issued: no dma-buf on Haiku).
---
diff --git a/third_party/wayland-protocols/BUILD.gn b/third_party/wayland-protocols/BUILD.gn
index 7beb117..4656571 100644
--- a/third_party/wayland-protocols/BUILD.gn
+++ b/third_party/wayland-protocols/BUILD.gn
@@ -107,6 +107,11 @@ wayland_protocol("org_kde_kwin_idle") {
   sources = [ "kde/src/protocols/idle.xml" ]
 }
 
+# Chromium-HaikuOS: server-side decorations on Haiku.
+wayland_protocol("org_kde_kwin_server_decoration") {
+  sources = [ "kde/src/protocols/server-decoration.xml" ]
+}
+
 wayland_protocol("pointer_constraints_protocol") {
   sources =
       [ "src/unstable/pointer-constraints/pointer-constraints-unstable-v1.xml" ]
